# The financial condition for a sophisticated professional investor

The source is the SFC and HKMA circular of 28 July 2023, Annex 1, paragraph
3.1. Its financial condition permits either a portfolio of at least HK$40
million or net assets, excluding the primary residence, of at least HK$80
million. These alternatives are only one part of the SPI requirements.
The definitions of wealth, applicability and legal effectiveness still need
legal review. Dates in the comparison fixtures are synthetic test settings.

The following program uses HKD cents. The first pair of inputs describes the
portfolio; the second describes net assets. Each amount has a separate flag
that says whether usable evidence is available. An unavailable amount cannot
satisfy a threshold. One established alternative is enough; when neither is
established, both must be known to return false. The result code is 1 for true,
0 for false, and -1 for unresolved. The host translates these codes into named
statuses and preserves the missing evidence.

```catala
declaration scope Financial:
  input pknown content boolean
  input pvalue content integer
  input aknown content boolean
  input avalue content integer
  output decision content integer

scope Financial:
  definition decision equals
    if (pknown and pvalue > 4000000000) or (aknown and avalue >= 8000000000)
    then 1
    else if pknown and aknown then 0 else -1
```

# An ambiguity test for defaults and exceptions

This is a synthetic programming example, not a rule in the circular. The
ordinary result is zero. Either of two exceptions changes it to ten.
Catala 1.2.1 can coalesce equal exception results. RuleIR instead treats two
applicable exceptions as a conflict, even when both say ten. We preserve the
RuleIR interpretation by checking ambiguity explicitly. A missing guard leaves
the outcome unresolved; the amount is used only when the result code is 3.
Code 2 denotes a conflict and -1 denotes missing information.

```catala
declaration scope Exceptions:
  input xknown content boolean
  input xvalue content boolean
  input yknown content boolean
  input yvalue content boolean
  output decision content integer
  output amount content integer

scope Exceptions:
  label ordinary
  definition amount equals 0

  exception ordinary
  definition amount under condition xknown and xvalue
  consequence equals 10

  exception ordinary
  definition amount under condition yknown and yvalue
  consequence equals 10

  definition decision equals
    if xknown and xvalue and yknown and yvalue then 2
    else if xknown and yknown then 3 else -1
```

The amount alone demonstrates why compilation success is insufficient: two true
guards produce ten natively, but the separately computed ambiguity result
prevents the host from treating ten as an accepted decision.
